Add Deployment Configuration: If not already configured, run the command npx fiori add deploy-config in your project terminal. Select Cloud Foundry as the target environment.
Build the Project: Generate a Multi-Target Application (MTA) archive by right-clicking the mta.yaml file and selecting Build MTA Project, or run npm run build in the terminal.
Deploy the Archive: Once the .mtar file is generated in the mta_archives folder, right-click it and select Deploy MTA Archive. This uploads your application to the HTML5 Application Repository in your BTP subaccount. 
